Subject: [PATCH] VBA: an object variable given a value keeps working

The link for class events read an object from what an assignment set, which
raised error 91 when d("a") = 1 stored a number through Dim d As Object.
---
--- a/basic/source/runtime/runtime.cxx
+++ b/basic/source/runtime/runtime.cxx
@@ -1965,7 +1965,7 @@
             *refVar = *refVal;
         }
         // HST: for RaiseEvent: an object of a class module set to a variable whose module has handlers
-        if( bVBAEnabled && !dynamic_cast<SbProcedureProperty*>( refVar.get() ) )
+        if( bVBAEnabled && refVar->GetType() == SbxOBJECT && !dynamic_cast<SbProcedureProperty*>( refVar.get() ) )
         {
             if( SbxObject* pSource = dynamic_cast<SbClassModuleObject*>( refVar->GetObject() ) )
             {
